cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use swingbus in your work, please cite it with these metadata.
title: "swingbus: power flow, contingency analysis and DC optimal power flow in Python"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Essamit
    given-names: Elmehdi
repository-code: https://github.com/akeanti/swingbus
url: https://github.com/akeanti/swingbus
abstract: >-
  swingbus is a Python library for steady-state analysis of transmission
  grids. It reads MATPOWER case files and provides Newton-Raphson,
  fast-decoupled, Gauss-Seidel and DC power flow, PTDF and LODF
  sensitivity factors, DC and AC N-1 contingency screening, DC optimal
  power flow with locational marginal prices, economic dispatch, and a DC
  cascading failure simulator for building graph datasets. Results are
  validated against PYPOWER on the IEEE and PGLib-OPF test systems.
keywords:
  - power systems
  - power flow
  - optimal power flow
  - contingency analysis
  - cascading failures
  - locational marginal prices
  - MATPOWER
  - PGLib-OPF
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-05"
